# JRebirth Boundaries

Always prefer mechanisms framework already provides over ad-hoc shortcuts JRebirth has thread management wave-based messaging role split precisely so do not need shortcuts

## Shortcuts banned default

- No `new Thread(...)` normal application flow JRebirth routes work through internal thread manager Creating raw threads bypasses manager breaks concurrency guarantees makes lifecycle uncontrollable Use Service instead

- No `Platform.runLater(...)` used design pattern A single `runLater` fix one-off edge case may acceptable but using recurring pattern signals UI state mutated wrong thread Restructure let Model own state update through waves or commands

- No heavy business logic placed inside View or Controller Views build nodes Controllers wire events Business rules validation orchestration belong Model or Commands

- No stateful bindings owned View when belong Model If binding outlives single render pass or needs observed other components belongs Model

- No `localFacade().globalFacade()` access except rare hard integration cases Accessing global facade directly breaks component isolation JRebirth provides Communicate through Waves instead

## When doubt

Stop read relevant role skill before writing more code A few minutes reading skill cheaper than refactoring broken design later
